<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvar Núñez Cabeza de Vaca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1490–c. 1559</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Cabeza de Vaca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvar Núñez Cabeza de Vaca was a Spanish explorer, one of four survivors of the Narváez expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> of 1527, who wandered for eight years across what is now the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>; his account is a key source on its peoples. As governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> from 1542 he reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a> overland, but he was deposed in 1544 and sent back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvar-nunez-cabeza-de-vaca.jpg" alt="Álvar Núñez Cabeza de Vaca" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ealmagro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cabeza_de_Vaca1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
